# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Nothing here is required. Every setting below is opt-in, and the core install
# runs with an empty file — that is deliberate, because a system whose default
# path needs a credential cannot be verified by someone who does not have one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — optional. Enables the language-model half of two commands.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   xg discover --llm     also asks a model for feature hypotheses. Its
#                         proposals pass exactly the same parse, static
#                         validation and leakage gates as the deterministic
#                         generator's, so the key buys more candidates, never a
#                         lower bar. Without a key the request is skipped, the
#                         deterministic generator runs alone, and the run
#                         completes — you are told the key was missing rather
#                         than the flag being silently honoured.
#
#   xg team-news          reads a model for club news the FPL API has not
#                         published. Without a key it prints the shortlist it
#                         would have searched, says plainly that no key was
#                         found, files nothing, and exits non-zero. Every
#                         existing recommendation is left exactly as it was —
#                         the deterministic `xg refresh` path covers everything
#                         official and needs no credential at all.
#
# Needs the optional extra as well: `uv sync --all-packages --extra llm`.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XG_ALONSO_OFFLINE — set to any non-empty value to forbid every outbound
# request. `xg ingest` then raises rather than reaching the network. `xg demo`
# is expected to pass with this set; that is how the offline path is tested.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# XG_ALONSO_OFFLINE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XG_MODEL_PATH — optional. Points the HTTP API (`make api`) at a trained
# artifact. Unset, the API serves the closed-form baseline instead of refusing
# to start.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# XG_MODEL_PATH=.data/models/component_models.pkl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XG_ALONSO_FIXTURES — optional. Where `xg demo` looks for the committed demo
# fixtures. Only needed for a non-editable install, where `data/fixtures` is
# not reachable from the imported package.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# XG_ALONSO_FIXTURES=./data/fixtures
